1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,160
The third floor of the dungeon.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:10,720
After you go through the graveyard in the tallest tower's forest, you'll arrive inside the golden castle.

3
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:17,560
Once opulent, the interior is now covered in dust and mold, a shadow of its former glory.

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,120
Deep within, footsteps echo through the halls.

5
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:27,200
They could belong to another adventurer, or to a former resident, now undead.

6
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,020
That there's a skeleton.

7
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,160
That's a human.

8
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:38,760
That's a ghoul.

9
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:40,860
You're weirdly accurate, but how?

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,820
The footsteps of people, skeletons, and zombies all sound totally different.

11
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:53,020
We'll go left. There are golems down that other corridor.

12
00:00:53,020 --> 00:01:00,500
Golems. Magical creatures made from mud, dirt, and stone, and humanoid in shape.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,960
Puppets that follow their creators every order.

14
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:05,000
Wait.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,120
Before you say it, we are not eating golems.

16
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,920
They're 99% rocks and dirt.

17
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,700
They're not alive. They're magical.

18
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,860
Heck, even I can make one of them.

19
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,280
Teach me how.

20
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:16,740
No.

21
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:19,760
If she taught you how, we all know what you'd do with it.

22
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:23,260
If there's golems down there, I need to get some things from them.

23
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:24,540
Follow me.

24
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:28,880
My base camp.

25
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,360
It's not much, but make yourselves to home.

26
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:32,560
Whoa.

27
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,060
Do you live here?

28
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,060
Nah, I don't sleep here much.

29
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:40,400
I do my hunting on the second and fourth floors.

30
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:45,820
Around about every month or so, I go to the village to get spice and other stuff I'm low on.

31
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,780
In fact, I ran into you on my way back from a supply run.

32
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,560
There's not much to eat here on the third.

33
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:57,520
Most of the monsters you find are either rotting away or just bones walking around.

34
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,480
But we got golems.

35
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,820
Hoo boy, they are something special.

36
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:07,760
Their bodies are filled with nutrients, and they maintain a consistent temperature and humidity.

37
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,640
A useful critter if there ever was one.

38
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,900
So what you're saying is...

39
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,060
You use them as a walking veggie patch?

40
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,460
That's an affront to farming!

41
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:19,720
And to magic scoloring, too!

42
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,000
What's the harm?

43
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,940
I might not like magic much, but I dang well appreciate golems.

44
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:27,820
They're a whole lot better than your average cropland.

45
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,020
Bugs are never a problem, because they kill them all.

46
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,460
They deal with vegetable thieves, too.

47
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,740
Who'd steal veggies off a golem?

48
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:39,160
They keep their water levels perfect so they don't dry out.

49
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:42,380
And anything you plant on them is guaranteed to grow.

50
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,240
They do all the hard work for you.

51
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:47,660
But like any field of crops, they need tendon now and again.

52
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:50,320
That's how come I set up my base camp here.

53
00:02:54,940 --> 00:03:07,640
No way!

54
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,660
What are you gonna do?

55
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:10,660
Should we help?

56
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:11,080
Nope!

57
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:31,360
That's amazing.

58
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,820
He knows how to handle them.

59
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:36,600
How does he know where the magic cores are to disable them?

60
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,680
I think I know how.

61
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,080
All done.

62
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,400
You mind helping me harvest all the veggies off them?

63
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,960
I couldn't even tell these were gardens on their backs at first.

64
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:51,520
Since the plants live on the golems, are they, like, parasites to them?

65
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:52,640
Nope.

66
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,320
It's a symbiotic kind of thing.

67
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:59,000
Once the plants take root, they hold the dirt together and make the golem's body stronger.

68
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,160
Really?

69
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,660
Give me a hand pulling up these weeds.

70
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:11,760
Now that's a harvest!

71
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,980
Finally, we get to eat some normal vegetables!

72
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,920
Set the weeds over here so they can dry out.

73
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,080
Dead weeds make great fertilizer.

74
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:24,400
In fact, I got a batch ready from last time that I'll bury in the golems now.

75
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:25,300
Huh?

76
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,800
These jars are filled with a different kind of fertilizer.

77
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,560
I give the golem a splash of it, and it's good to go.

78
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,960
I knew it!

79
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:34,780
Knew what?

80
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,500
That's how you knew where the golem's cores were.

81
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,400
You plant them back each time yourself.

82
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,460
It is a crime, you know.

83
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:44,220
Tampering with magical creatures without permission.

84
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:45,760
What crime?

85
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,780
I'm just tilling soil and tending a farm.

86
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,980
An illegal golem farm.

87
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,840
Till the soil up good and dig some ridges.

88
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,680
Also, never plant the same thing in the golem you got it from.

89
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,220
Rotating crops keeps the soil working right.

90
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,480
I'm so tired.

91
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:07,460
I felt like it took more effort than fighting monsters.

92
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:11,520
Thanks to all your help, it got done faster than if I did it myself.

93
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,360
I drank so much water, I need to pee.

94
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,060
All right.

95
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,240
While the elf girl's in the bathroom,

96
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:22,980
do me another favor and help me sweep up this extra dirt.

97
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:32,680
Taro, Jiro, Saburo.

98
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,780
Do they revive right away after you bury them?

99
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:38,400
No, it takes a little while.

100
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,800
The roots need time to grow enough

101
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,460
so the dirt doesn't come apart when the golem gets up and moves.

102
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:50,360
You really do care a lot about these golems.

103
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,400
That's so amazing.

104
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,820
And you've been doing this all by yourself.

105
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,740
Hasn't that been difficult?

106
00:05:58,140 --> 00:05:59,840
Nothing hard about it at all.

107
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,840
It's a thing I like doing.

108
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:06,480
We're all done.

109
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:10,680
Now, let's have a feast of all the stuff we worked so hard to get.

110
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:15,080
What a beautiful color.

111
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,400
Guess I'm the expert at peeling things now.

112
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,100
You want it smaller or is it okay?

113
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,700
Nah, that's perfect.

114
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,060
Need to light that fire?

115
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,060
I can do it.

116
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:31,060
I got my striker and flint for that.

117
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:34,000
You don't have to light it that way all the time.

118
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:35,900
It'd be faster with magic.

119
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:39,080
How can you light golems and be anti-magic?

120
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:41,440
Every time you do a thing the easy way,

121
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,240
it dulls your skill for doing it.

122
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,520
Convenient and simple ain't the same.

123
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,680
Doing things your way with magic

124
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,000
is the same as buying veggies at the store.

125
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:51,260
Hmm.

126
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:59,160
This is the last of the basilisk bacon.

127
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,120
It's ready.

128
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,920
Thank you for the meal.

129
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:17,800
This is so good!

130
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,660
How can something that grows underground be this delicious?

131
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,000
Maybe the veggies taste so good

132
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,300
because of something in the golem.

133
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,060
Shut it!

134
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,480
I don't care if it walks.

135
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,960
It's just a veggie patch.

136
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,220
By the way,

137
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,320
if a golem's body is 99% dirt,

138
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,560
what's the last 1% of it?

139
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,220
That secret.

140
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:38,900
Ah!

141
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,420
That hit the spot.

142
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,600
I'm so stuffed.

143
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,520
I feel like taking a nap now.

144
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:46,980
Go on and take one.

145
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:50,040
I got a few chores I need to do anyway.

146
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,600
Hmm.

147
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:53,220
Help clean up.

148
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:54,320
Gonna hit the head.

149
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:58,360
I appreciate having a nice, clean bathroom way down here.

150
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:01,560
It's so much better than your typical hole dug in the ground.

151
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,680
In a dungeon where there's a lot of foot traffic,

152
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,260
there are designated areas for restrooms.

153
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,400
They're always so well-maintained.

154
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,100
Some of them even have fresh flowers in them.

155
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,080
I wonder who goes to all the trouble.

156
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:19,300
Senshi!

157
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:22,020
What is it?

158
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,160
What are you doing?

159
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:27,440
I'm gonna fill up my fertilizer pots with the slop from the toilets.

160
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,460
I can't believe you can do that after eating.

161
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,120
This is the best fertilizer we have down here.

162
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,020
And the veggies we ate were...

163
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,360
Get a grip.

164
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:39,500
That's how it's done up top, too.

165
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:40,860
Yeah, I know.

166
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:42,220
It's still gross.

167
00:08:42,220 --> 00:08:43,440
Hey, Senshi.

168
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:44,000
Hang on.

169
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,040
Why do you go to all this trouble to live down here?

170
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,300
No offense, but life's easier up top.

171
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:52,080
You can still be self-sufficient

172
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,300
and do all your farming and hunting and stuff like that.

173
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,700
If I lived up there,

174
00:08:57,940 --> 00:09:00,540
who'd keep the bathrooms clean and stocked down here?

175
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:04,340
When a zombie's stuck in a toilet, who'd pull it out?

176
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,220
Who'd fix the golems if they fell apart?

177
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:11,200
You know, there used to be ten walking around.

178
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:13,300
But now, there's only three.

179
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:16,200
If they're gone, the monsters from the lower floors

180
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,820
would find their way up here.

181
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,320
That'll force the monsters that live here now

182
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,580
to go who knows where.

183
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:25,220
And those monsters will force other monsters out of their homes.

184
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:29,000
If that happens, this place will change in a bad way.

185
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:31,780
You won't be able to hunt or even walk around.

186
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,940
In dungeons, the same as a field.

187
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:37,000
If you don't take care of it right,

188
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:39,020
you can't enjoy what it brings you.

189
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:43,080
My thinking is, in here, I eat what I grow or hunt.

190
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:45,220
But I always give something back to it.

191
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:47,960
Living like that makes me appreciate the dungeon.

192
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,300
Makes me feel like when I step foot in here,

193
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:52,060
I'm a part of it all.

194
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,780
And that makes me happy.

195
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,200
But if that's the case,

196
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:02,020
is it okay to leave here to help us on our journey?

197
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,580
Won't this fall apart without you?

198
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:07,520
Nope, I don't have to be here all the time.

199
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:10,640
The golems can take care of things for a month or two.

200
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:14,620
Besides, if you folks up and died of malnutrition,

201
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:15,560
I'd feel terrible.

202
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,120
Wait here for me.

203
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,500
I'll be done in a bit.

204
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:26,300
Senshi is so amazing.

205
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:32,520
What are we doing, carrying all of this?

206
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:35,080
I use them to barter with.

207
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:37,480
Used to sell them from a stand where I'd leave them,

208
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,800
but that didn't work out.

209
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:40,740
You just left them there?

210
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,700
Honor system.

211
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,300
I had a treasure chest there to drop your money,

212
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:47,480
but the cash got stolen, so I stopped doing that.

213
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:51,440
No wonder that treasure chest always had money in it.

214
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,880
Is this floor the only one you do your bartering on?

215
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,800
My usual customers are down a few floors.

216
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:00,540
We set up a time to meet so they won't be there now.

217
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,340
I didn't want to leave these rotten on the golems,

218
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,160
but if we can't trade them off,

219
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,220
we'll just have to toss them.

220
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,220
Oh, well.

221
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,840
That is out of the question.

222
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,220
We can't waste this food.

223
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,400
After all the work it took to grow,

224
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,840
it's perfect and shiny and delicious.

225
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:15,860
Veggie lover.

226
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,340
Let's keep going.

227
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,720
With any luck,

228
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,880
we'll find someone on this floor who wants them.

229
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,960
This'll take forever.

230
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,540
Even in a dungeon,

231
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:28,560
there are merchants.

232
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:33,780
Enter.

233
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,700
Their customers are adventurers

234
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,960
and those who cannot return to the surface

235
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:44,160
for various reasons.

236
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:49,400
Welcome, good folk.

237
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:49,820
Welcome.

238
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,660
Will we be dining in or staying the night?

239
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:54,000
We're here to trade.

240
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,760
Ah, splendid, splendid.

241
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:58,920
And what are we trading today?

242
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,120
Vegetables.

243
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,140
Get out, go on, cat!

244
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:05,580
But, sir, just listen.

245
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,860
If you want to trade something, bring gold!

246
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:08,560
Understand?

247
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,320
You do know what gold is.

248
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,420
It's round and shiny and glitters!

249
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,240
We don't want gems or anything valuable.

250
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:18,100
Just some food and spices from your kitchen.

251
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:20,060
Look, isn't this round and shiny?

252
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,160
Show this here carrot to your cook.

253
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,480
They'll want to make something good out of it for sure.

254
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:25,460
That's disgusting!

255
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:27,220
Who the hell would want to eat that?

256
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:30,280
You rotten little...

257
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,900
If you treat food like that,

258
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,760
I swear you'll get yours in the end!

259
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,440
What are you waiting for?

260
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,200
Throw these idiots out of here already!

261
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,020
Just listen!

262
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,180
Orcs!

263
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,800
First ones to die are the ones with the weapons!

264
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:51,440
Go!

265
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:51,980
Kill them!

266
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:53,320
Kill every one of them!

267
00:12:53,320 --> 00:13:00,100
Why are orcs here?

268
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,460
They're supposed to live on the lower floors!

269
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:04,000
Who cares about that?

270
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,320
We have to...

271
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:10,060
Marcel!

272
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:20,280
What do you think you're doing hanging around a dump like this, Senshi?

273
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:23,920
I was gonna ask you the same thing.

274
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:28,520
You in a party with this lot?

275
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,800
That's right.

276
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,160
Humans and elves.

277
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:35,660
Don't tell me your usual customers.

278
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:36,780
Yep.

279
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,440
It's them.

280
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:42,120
I had a feeling he did business with a rough crowd.

281
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:42,940
But orcs?

282
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,800
I thought they'd be goblins.

283
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:45,580
Really?

284
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:47,100
I was sure they'd be kobolds.

285
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,700
I seen the red dragon.

286
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:53,720
The damn thing used to keep to itself.

287
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,140
Not anymore.

288
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:57,380
He's been showing up near our village,

289
00:13:57,660 --> 00:14:00,100
sniffing around and blowing fire all over.

290
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:03,480
We gots kids and old orcs to take cares of.

291
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:04,840
They can't fight,

292
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,360
so we came up to this floor till the dragon left.

293
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:09,500
You think that could be our dragon?

294
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:10,300
Tell me.

295
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,620
Where did you see it?

296
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,460
You think I'd tell you,

297
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,500
a human, where our village is?

298
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,080
Fat chance.

299
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,680
Chief, we done killing everyone.

300
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,000
Ah, great.

301
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,240
Pack up whatever's not nailed down, then.

302
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:25,060
What is this, milk?

303
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:27,580
It's rotten.

304
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:28,820
Chuck it.

305
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:31,940
Them veggies be something you grew, I guess.

306
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,960
We're on a supply run looking for food.

307
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,560
Appreciate if you'd share that with us.

308
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,920
Sure, be happy to.

309
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:40,920
What you got to trade for it?

310
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:41,940
No trade.

311
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,260
Tribe's desperate.

312
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,380
We barely got up to this floor alive.

313
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:50,060
You've been a good friend and I hate to do this,

314
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:53,760
but hand over everything you got right now.

315
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,600
Can't you reason with him?

316
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,300
All right.

317
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:00,880
Glad to hear that.

318
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:03,880
I want to ask you for a favor in return, though.

319
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:07,340
Let me and my party spend a night with your tribe.

320
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,220
What?

321
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:11,240
Do me that favor and you can have my veggies,

322
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:13,460
my life, hell, anything you want.

323
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:14,160
Huh?

324
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,540
Also, you there.

325
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:16,000
Me?

326
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,160
That stuff's not rotten, it's fermented.

327
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,720
Don't you dare throw it away.

328
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:20,260
Bring it.

329
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:26,100
They took all our weapons away.

330
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,760
How could you put us in this position?

331
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,380
If we find out where they set their camp up,

332
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:32,380
we'll never see the surface again.

333
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:34,020
Tell me you have a plan.

334
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,160
Please tell me you got a plan.

335
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,160
Mm-hmm.

336
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,980
That jar I told the orc not to throw out's got yeast in it.

337
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:41,640
Yeast is a leavening agent.

338
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:43,940
And I don't know if you noticed,

339
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:47,620
but the orcs also grabbed every sack of flour in the kitchen.

340
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:49,560
You know what that means, don't you?

341
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:50,980
Uh, no.

342
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:53,800
We can make bread!

343
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,000
Dummy!

344
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,440
Wait, so you don't have bread!

345
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,560
I don't know how stupid you are!

346
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:58,960
You don't have bread!

347
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,260
Not one bread!

348
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,740
Fight down, you savages!

349
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:06,580
Is that an elf?

350
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,380
What a barbaric face.

351
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,860
You have to stay in this pen.

352
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:12,820
Dad's back from pillaging.

353
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:17,220
We won't end up as ingredients in their dinner, will we?

354
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:19,980
What did you do with that jar of leavening agent?

355
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:20,540
Huh?

356
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:23,320
You don't know what it is, you don't know how to use it,

357
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:24,180
so give it to me!

358
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:25,200
Come on!

359
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,000
I can make bread with it!

360
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:27,760
Bread!

361
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:28,280
Bread!

362
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:28,800
Bread!

363
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:29,320
Bread!

364
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:29,740
Bread!

365
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:29,800
Bread!

366
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:35,740
Put flour, salt, sugar, leavening agent, and water in a bowl.

367
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:36,880
Then knead it.

368
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:39,300
Work that sucker till it's nice and firm.

369
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:42,060
Are you playing with mud?

370
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,140
Uh, huh?

371
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,660
Time for your history lesson, kiddo.

372
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:52,440
In the old days, we lived up top, not here in the underground, like the bugs.

373
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:59,100
Humans and elves like those ones murdered most of our kin and stole the land we had up there.

374
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:03,280
I seem to remember orcs did a whole lot of murdering, too.

375
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,040
Was that?

376
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,360
Now's a good time to add the olive oil.

377
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:13,520
Anyway, they chased us down to the underground, and our tribe found a new home.

378
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:18,360
For a long time, we lived in peace, till their kind found us again.

379
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:22,940
To knead, you hold the edge, then smack it down again and again.

380
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:26,460
They poured oil in our caves and set fire to it.

381
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:31,900
That's because your people wouldn't stop raiding the villages of every other race in the land.

382
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,640
We was doing what we had to to survive.

383
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:37,960
All orcs ever did was rob and kill and terrorize everyone.

384
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:39,600
That's why you were chased here.

385
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,680
Come on, Marsau, stop it.

386
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:42,660
We're their guests.

387
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:43,540
Shut your hole!

388
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:46,520
Get your fingers in there and work that dough!

389
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:47,180
Sorry.

390
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:48,920
Give me that.

391
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:49,860
I'll do it.

392
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,300
Your kind chased my tribe underground.

393
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:56,140
We found this dungeon and made it our home, and you come here to steal it.

394
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:00,120
It was the villagers who were the first to discover this dungeon.

395
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,320
But us orcs were the first to come down this deep.

396
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:06,260
If that's where you want to go with it, then zombies were here first!

397
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:09,460
Once you get it stretching easy, it's time for the first proofing.

398
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:15,680
When the dough gets twice as big, cut it into equal pieces.

399
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,240
Then shape with your hands.

400
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:20,780
Why you been so quiet, Tallman?

401
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,040
Huh?

402
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,140
Don't you have no opinion on things?

403
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:30,080
Rumors say if a body defeats the mad mage that built this dungeon, a body gets to rule the castle.

404
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:33,680
You must be here to get to the bottom of this dungeon.

405
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:38,480
When you get your kingdom, what you gonna do then?

406
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:44,460
I know all about that rumor, too, but I never thought about it that much.

407
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:46,480
Typical adventurer.

408
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:49,540
If I cut down to the bone, you're all the same.

409
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:51,640
A bunch of greedy idiots.

410
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:54,480
All you care about is gold and power.

411
00:18:55,040 --> 00:19:00,200
The thought someone like that could rule this place makes my hair stand up all prickly-like.

412
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:04,720
That's how come if we see a surface dweller down here, we'd kill him.

413
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:05,980
Okay, that does it!

414
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,800
If you're so noble, take over the castle yourself!

415
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:11,660
Or is stealing stuff the only thing orcs are good at doing?

416
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,160
You got guts, elf girl.

417
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:15,760
I like you.

418
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,040
I'm gonna throw you in the fire myself!

419
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:20,920
See? The only thing you know how to do is violence!

420
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,520
Let it prove some more.

421
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:31,000
Then, once it finishes rising, set it down over some low heat.

422
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:39,480
Steam it for a little bit, and when you open the lid, we got ourselves some bread!

423
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:41,580
It smells amazing!

424
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,380
Let's have a taste.

425
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:48,620
Hold it! That bread belongs to my tribe, and we're not giving you any.

426
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:49,380
What?

427
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:53,040
You said you wanted to make bread, and we let you make it.

428
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,400
But we decide what to do with it.

429
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:58,320
Daddy?

430
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,040
Hmm?

431
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,040
We all made it together.

432
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:03,500
Why can't we all eat it together, too?

433
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:10,020
It's not a proper meal if you only have bread.

434
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:13,260
Main dish, side dish, and veggies.

435
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,700
You need all of those for a balanced meal.

436
00:20:15,700 --> 00:20:19,860
Your daddy there? He just wanted to wait until all the other dishes were ready.

437
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,540
Hold your tongue, elf!

438
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:22,780
She's right.

439
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:26,720
Your pop said we could stay with your family if we let him have our vegetables.

440
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:30,440
And your daddy's an orc who always keeps his word.

441
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:35,680
Hey!

442
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:37,780
Get them whatever they need.

443
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:47,640
There. It's ready.

444
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:49,860
Eat up!

445
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,040
It looks yummy.

446
00:20:51,040 --> 00:21:00,200
Whoa, it's good!

447
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,920
It's good and spicy!

448
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:09,820
We used the same ingredients as we did for your stewed cabbage, but this tastes totally different.

449
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:13,120
Before, I said orcs are only good at stealing.

450
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,280
But you're pretty good cooks, too.

451
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:17,080
Shudderholm.

452
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:22,940
Um, earlier you asked why I wanted to get to the bottom of the dungeon.

453
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,020
My sister was eaten by a red dragon.

454
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,460
And we're just trying to find it.

455
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:33,720
But if you can tell us where you saw it, we can go find it and kill it.

456
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:37,120
We won't go near your village or tell anyone about it.

457
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:43,340
I swear.

458
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:49,120
Hey!

459
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:50,740
Get me that map!

460
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:51,360
On it!

461
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:57,440
We saw it two floors down from here, near the living quarters on the west side.

462
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,240
Thanks a lot.

463
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:02,800
Hmm.

464
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:09,760
From now on, I promise I'll think hard about what to do if I end up ruling the castle.

465
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:10,780
Ha!

466
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:16,020
To think a guy caught by orcs and forced to make bread could ever be a king of anything.

467
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:19,120
Well, good luck to you.

468
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:22,920
Thanks, that's funny.

469
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:24,920
Ow!

470
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:29,920
Did you know that cabbage was grown on the back of a golem?

471
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:37,940
Opinions may differ, but we can all agree, we get hungry.

472
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,880
Delicious dungeon food brings folks together.

473
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:44,820
Delicious in dungeon.

